cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "massive-binary-sim: a physically-traceable simulation framework for a bound pair of massive stars"
abstract: >-
  A modular framework for the evolution of a gravitationally bound pair of
  massive stars (8-150 solar masses each). Every equation is traceable to a
  cited source; competing physical prescriptions (winds, convection, mass
  transfer stability, common-envelope formalism, supernova engine, gravity
  order) are selectable at runtime; every coefficient is exposed with its
  literature range. Ships a validation suite against analytic solutions and
  the Hulse-Taylor pulsar. The stellar-evolution component uses reduced
  fitting relations, not a stellar-structure integration; see KNOWN_GAPS.md.
